WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
The light we see from one galaxy
left it about 260 million years ago.

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.990
And that galaxy, like the
others far beyond our own,

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.910
is moving away from us.

4
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.600
Rewind time, and every
galaxy moves closer.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.180
Were they once all together?

6
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.190
And can we work out how long ago that was?

7
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.710
In this mission, you'll meet Hubble's law,

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.160
and the constant at its
heart: the Hubble constant.

9
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.170
Then you'll use it to work
out how far away a galaxy is.

10
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.710
Your mission: decide whether we can work
out when the galaxies were all together,

11
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:34.510
and how.
